   "evidence": "Diff lines 359\u2013361: `@[simp] theorem piMinus_eq_chargeConj_piPlus : piMinus = piPlus.chargeConj := (rfl)` and `@[simp] theorem kMinus_eq_chargeConj_kPlus : kMinus = kPlus.chargeConj := (rfl)`; no `piMinus_*`/`kMinus_*` projection lemmas exist in the file (grep `piMinus_` hits only the `_eq_chargeConj_` lemma and the `isChargeConsistent_piMinus` proof that rewrites through it).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Meson/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `@[simp]` from both `_eq_chargeConj_` lemmas (keep them as plain `(rfl)` restatements), and add the projection simp lemmas that `piPlus`/`kPlus` already have: `piMinus_valenceQuark : piMinus.valenceQuark = d`, `piMinus_valenceAntiquark = u`, `piMinus_charge = -1`, `piMinus_mass`, `piMinus_decayConstant`, and the same five for `kMinus` (with `s`, `u`, `-1`).",
   "issue": "`@[simp] piMinus_eq_chargeConj_piPlus : piMinus = piPlus.chargeConj` (and `kMinus_eq_chargeConj_kPlus` at line 361) are simp lemmas whose LHS is a bare constant, so every `simp` call rewrites `piMinus`/`kMinus` away into `piPlus.chargeConj`/`kPlus.chargeConj`. The named mesons that 1.3 and 1.4 state relations over (e.g. a density of the negative pion) then cannot survive `simp` as subjects; this is exposing the body through simp instead of supplying the projection API.",
   "line": 359
  }
 ],
